  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to \\pi }{csc}^{2}\u2061(\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$",
  "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=\\pi $ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\pi }{csc}^{2}\u2061(\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & ={csc}^{2}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & ={csc}^{2}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
